# Zero-Terminal Deployment Plan

The goal is to make the GHG Reporting Platform 100% "Plug and Play" for hosts where the user cannot access a terminal.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/server.js)
- **Auto-Seed on Startup**: On launch, the server will check if [users_v2.db](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/users_v2.db) exists. If not, it will automatically invoke the seeding logic.
- **Dependency Awareness**: The platform is already using `bcryptjs` (pure JavaScript), which is safer for cross-platform uploads than the binary-based `bcrypt`.
- **Port Configurability**: Uses `process.env.PORT` to satisfy cloud platform requirements.

### [MODIFY] [seed_script.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/seed_script.js)
- **Module Export**: Wrap the main seeding logic in an exported function `runSeed(callback)` so [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/server.js) can trigger it programmatically.

### [MODIFY] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/package.json)
- **Main Entry**: Confirmed as [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/server.js).

## Deployment Guide for No-Terminal Hosts
1. **Modern Hosts (Render, Heroku, Railway, Vercel)**:
   - They **automatically** run `npm install` when they see your [package.json](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/package.json).
   - The server will boot, see no database, and run the seed script automatically.
   - **Status: Ready.**
2. **Classic/Shared Hosts (cPanel, Plesk)**:
   - Look for a "Node.js Selector" or "Setup Node.js App" icon.
   - Click the button labeled **"Run NPM Install"** in that UI.

## Verification Plan
1. Delete local [.db](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/test.db) files.
2. Run `npm start`.
3. Verify that the platform initializes itself and the `test` user works immediately.
